# Each part of the platform has its own env file, next to its code. Copy each example and fill it in:
#
#   bridge/.env.example             -> bridge/.env               Postgres, MinIO, Kafka (docker compose)
#   server/.env.example             -> server/.env               core API: database, storage, Kafka, secrets, intake & publishing connections
#   agentic_framework/.env.example  -> agentic_framework/.env    the agent: model provider and API keys, limits
#   www/.env.example                -> www/.env.local            web app: where the API runs
#
# Database and MinIO credentials must be the same in bridge/, server/ and agentic_framework/.
# Real .env files hold secrets: never commit them.
